<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  FALCON V2 - ACTUATOR STANDALONE BENCH world (gazebo-testing, 2026-09-12).

  Purpose: STEP 4 of ACTUATOR_CONTROL_LIMIT_CYCLE_FIX_AND_VALIDATION - a
  NO-FLIGHT, single-surface actuator step-response bench used by
  tests/gazebo/scripts/test_actuator_standalone_step_response.py.

  CLASSIFICATION: TEMPORARY_TEST_SETUP / MEASUREMENT-ONLY.
  This world MODIFIES NO AIRCRAFT PHYSICS PARAMETER. It contains no mass, CG,
  inertia, aerodynamic, propulsion or actuator value of any kind. It only
  chooses which model package to spawn, where, and under what gravity.

  DERIVATION FROM AN EXISTING WORLD - exactly two differences from
  tests/gazebo/worlds/falcon_v2_freefall_world.sdf, disclosed in full
  (this list includes the comment-header difference, per validation finding
  m12, 2026-09-11):

    (a) THIS COMMENT HEADER differs (the freefall world's 22-line header is
        replaced by this 60-line one). Comments only - no element value.
    (b) <world name> : falcon_v2_freefall_test
                    -> falcon_v2_actuator_standalone_bench
    (c) <include><uri> : file:///home/emirhan/Desktop/FalconV2/model
                      -> file:///home/emirhan/Desktop/FalconV2/tests/gazebo/models/falcon_v2_highrate_diag
    (d) <include><pose> : 0 0 5 0 0 0  ->  0 0 100 0 0 0
    (e) the <model name="ground_plane"> block and the <light> block are
        REMOVED (no ground contact and no rendering is wanted on this bench).

  RATIONALE FOR EACH:
    (b) a distinct world name so no pre-existing world/result namespace is
        touched.
    (c) falcon_v2_highrate_diag is byte-identical to model/ except for two
        <diagnostics_rate_hz> PUBLISH RATES (20.0 -> 1000.0) - see that
        model's own header and docs/validation/2026-09-11_*.md finding m13,
        which independently established that BOTH the actuators plugin and
        the aerodynamics plugin apply their forces EVERY physics step and
        throttle only Publish(). 1 kHz diagnostics are required here because
        the quantities under test (rise time ~5-20 ms, rate-clamp duty,
        effort-clamp duty) are not resolvable at 20 Hz.
    (d) 100 m so the airframe can never reach the (now absent) ground during
        a 3.5 s case, and so no contact force can contaminate a hinge-torque
        measurement.
    (e) no ground plane -> no contact solver involvement at all; no light ->
        headless-clean.

  GRAVITY IS ON (0 0 -9.81), deliberately: the 2026-08-24 gravity-droop
  result being re-verified in this stage is a gravity-driven measurement, and
  the standalone bench must be able to reproduce it. The airframe's own
  body-frame velocity is held at zero by the test script (aero_lib.hold_step),
  so dynamic pressure is identically zero and the aerodynamics plugin
  contributes no force - the ONLY torques on the surface under test are its
  own actuator torque and its own weight about its hinge.

  No plugin is attached by this world; every plugin comes from the included
  model package, unmodified.
-->
<sdf version="1.9">
  <world name="falcon_v2_actuator_standalone_bench">
    <physics name="1ms" type="dartsim">
      <max_step_size>0.001</max_step_size>
      <real_time_factor>0</real_time_factor>
    </physics>
    <gravity>0 0 -9.81</gravity>

    <plugin filename="gz-sim-physics-system" name="gz::sim::systems::Physics"></plugin>
    <plugin filename="gz-sim-scene-broadcaster-system" name="gz::sim::systems::SceneBroadcaster"></plugin>

    <include>
      <uri>file:///home/emirhan/Desktop/FalconV2/tests/gazebo/models/falcon_v2_highrate_diag</uri>
      <name>falcon_v2</name>
      <pose>0 0 100 0 0 0</pose>
    </include>
  </world>
</sdf>
